cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Vx: a systems programming language for heterogeneous computing"
message: "If you use Vx or its documentation, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Vx Project"
    website: "https://vxlang.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vx-lang/Vx"
url: "https://vxlang.org"
abstract: >-
  Vx is a systems programming language for heterogeneous computing. CPU, GPU, NPU and
  accelerator memory are part of the type system, so a host thread dereferencing a device
  pointer is a compile error rather than a segfault. Placement, capacity and reachability
  are checked against a declared machine before a binary exists.
keywords:
  - compiler
  - programming language
  - heterogeneous computing
  - GPU
  - NPU
  - MLIR
  - type system
# CFF validates this against the SPDX identifier list, which has no entry for a "WITH"
# expression, so the exception is carried by the URL instead.
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://github.com/vx-lang/Vx/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: 0.0.1
